{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וכי תבאו מלחמה", :translit "v'chi tavo'u milchamah", :gloss "and when you go to war"} {:he "מלחמת גוג", :translit "milchemet gog", :gloss "war of Gog"} {:he "ימות המשיח", :translit "y'mot ha-mashiach", :gloss "days of the Messiah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Allusion: the verse's war foreshadows the eschatological war of Gog"}], :frame {:text "Ezekiel 38–39 describes the war of Gog of Magog in the end of days. The Talmud identifies this as the war preceding the messianic era (Megillah 11a; Sanhedrin 97a).", :sources ["Ezekiel 38:1–39:29" "Megillah 11a" "Sanhedrin 97a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "תבאו מלחמה", :translit "tavo'u milchamah", :gloss "you shall go to war"} {:he "במלחמת גוג", :translit "b'milchemet gog", :gloss "in the war of Gog"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "תבאו מלחמה", :b "במלחמת גוג"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "תבאו", :translit "tavo'u", :gloss "you shall go"} {:he "אבות", :translit "avot", :gloss "patriarchs"} {:he "זכות האבות", :translit "zechut ha-avot", :gloss "merit of the patriarchs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Permutation: תבאו rearranges to אבות"}], :frame {:text "The Mishnah states that the merit of the patriarchs protects Israel (Makkot 23b, Berachot 4a). The Yom Kippur liturgy invokes the merit of the patriarchs, citing Micah 7:20, \"Give truth to Jacob, kindness to Abraham.\" Rabbinic tradition extols Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob as the three patriarchs whose merit endures for their descendants (Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer 33).", :sources ["Makkot 23b" "Berachot 4a" "Micah 7:20" "Pirkei DeRabbi Eliezer 33"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והרעותם בחצוצרות", :translit "v'hra'otem b'chatzotzrot", :gloss "and you shall sound the trumpets"} {:he "רוע התרועעה הארץ תרועם בשבט ברזל", :translit "ro'a hitrata eretz t'roatzem b'shevet barzel", :gloss "You have made the earth tremble; You have broken it; with an iron scepter You shatter them"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the trumpet-blasting (הרעותם / תרועה) links to the trembling/shattering (רוע / תרועם) of Psalms 60:10"}], :frame {:text "Psalms 60:10 uses the root רוע in the sense of breaking and shattering the earth with an iron scepter. Ba'al HaTurim connects the trumpet sound commanded in Numbers 10:9 to this verse's language of divine shattering of enemies.", :sources ["Psalms 60:10" "Numbers 10:9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Allusion: the verse's war foreshadows the eschatological war of Gog", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "תבאו מלחמה", :a-value 532, :b "במלחמת גוג", :b-value 532, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :other, :note "Permutation: תבאו rearranges to אבות", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the trumpet-blasting (הרעותם / תרועה) links to the trembling/shattering (רוע / תרועם) of Psalms 60:10", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:06.164485454Z", :model "glm-5.2"}